Name: dav2d is an AV2 decoder :)
Short Name: dav2d
URL: https://code.videolan.org/videolan/dav2d
Version: 0.0.1
Revision: 5453e990e31cbb50eee06deb2da7876589d61c71
Update Mechanism: Manual (https://crbug.com/576731818)
License: BSD-2-Clause
License File: LICENSE
Security Critical: yes
Shipped: yes
CPEPrefix: cpe:/a:videolan:dav2d
Source: https://code.videolan.org/videolan/dav2d

Description:
This contains the source to the dav2d video decoder; used for AV2 decoding in
Chromium. The LICENSE file is copied from libdav2d/COPYING.

Security Considerations:
dav2d decodes untrusted AV2 video bitstreams from the internet and is written in
C and assembly. To mitigate memory safety risks, decoding runs only inside
sandboxed renderer processes, frame allocations are bounded by Chromium's
canvas size limits, and the decoder and container parsers are exercised by
fuzzers on ClusterFuzz.

Local Modifications:
None

--[ UPDATING ] ------------------
To update run "git pull" within the libdav2d directory to sync your local copy
of the checkout to upstream. Then you need to update the configuration files
and source listing.

First have clang (//third_party/llvm-build/Release+Asserts/bin), clang-cl
(https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/lkgr/docs/win_cross.md),
and meson v0.55 or higher (https://github.com/mesonbuild/meson/releases) in
your path. Then you can run ./generate_configs.py

Next you should update the dav2d_generated.gni file, to do that run the
./generate_source.py command.

Hopefully all that works and then you can roll DEPS to the new revision with
all the updated configuration files. If not, you'll need to debug the bots :(
